  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nWith the main system that brought the area rain today will\ncontinue to weaken today, with scattered rain showers expected\nmainly for the Catskills and NE PA. Additional rainfall amounts\nare only expected to be a tenth to a quarter inch. Otherwise,\nseasonable temperatures are expected today as well, with high\ntemperatures in the low to mid 60s. \n\nHigh pressure will slowly build into the region behind the departing \nsystem tonight. Winds will become calm, and with model \nsoundings showing low-level moisture in addition to any \nmoisture added from recent rainfall, this will likely lead to \nwidespread fog and/or low stratus tonight into Tuesday morning.\n\nHigh pressure will continue to build into the region on Tuesday,\nbringing a stretch of quieter weather conditions through \nmidweek. Southwest to westerly flow will advect in much warmer \nair and push daytime highs into the 70s. Valley locations may \neven reach 80 on Thursday.\n\nRain will return late in the week, though there remains \nuncertainty with timing. A broad low pressure system will set up\nover Canada. A frontal system will extend from the low all the \nway back into the Midwest. This frontal system will push in as \nearly as Thursday night and move through on Friday. While there \nare some timing differences, model guidance favor high pressure \nbuilding in early Saturday behind this front's departure which \nwould favor a dry yet cooler start to the weekend. High pressure\nwill stick around into Sunday though just how long it can delay\nthe arrival of the next system remains uncertain.",
